I love the rainbow that appears after a heavy summer shower. It is not just a picture in the sky; it feels like a secret promise.

The clouds are still grey and heavy, hanging low over the green hills. But then, the sun breaks through. A single beam of light hits the wet air. Suddenly, a bright arch appears. It stretches from the old oak tree in the garden to the top of the hill.

My favourite part is the red. It is deep and warm, like a cosy blanket. Next to it, the orange glows like a tiny fire. The yellow is bright, like a lemon sweet. Then comes the green, fresh like new grass. The blue is calm, like a quiet lake. Finally, the purple fades into the mist.

I run outside, my wellies splashing in puddles. I try to catch the end of the rainbow, but it always moves away. It is shy. It only stays for a few minutes. When it fades, the world looks cleaner and brighter. The smell of wet earth fills the air. I smile, knowing it will return after the next rain. It is nature’s most beautiful smile. [end of text]


